//   · assert -> exit code: `fn main() -> i32`
// ── BUCKET 2: re-ported as-is, still admitted, still a defect.
// ── ROOT RE-CHECKED AGAINST THE RESTORED CONSTRUCT, and it is NOT bck.C. The capture
//    is not invisible: what decides whether a `move` capture counts as a MOVE of the
//    captured local is the USE FORM INSIDE THE BODY, not the `move` keyword.
//    MEASURED ONE-VARIABLE PAIR on THIS program, 2026-09-07 — only the closure body
//    differs, everything else identical:
//      spawn(move || { let _ = *v; });   (deref READ)      -> ADMITS
//      spawn(move || { eat(v); });       (by-value use)    -> REFUSED,
//         "error [fn box_imm]: cannot move 'v' while it is borrowed"
//    So the loan on `v` IS live and the move check IS reached; the capture whose only
//    use is a read deposits no move. Upstream's body is `println!("v={}", *v)` — a
//    read — which is why the upstream program lands on the admitting side.
// ── ⚠ THIS ROW AND `borrowck-loan-blocks-move-cc--t10` ARE THE SAME CONSTRUCT TWICE.
//    Upstream's `box_imm` and `box_imm_explicit` are textually identical at this
